WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.859 --> 00:00:05.690
At this year's San Diego Comic-Con, DC Universe
drew back the curtain on its animated Harley

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:10.360
Quinn series — a hard-R romp revolving around
the off-the-rails rule-breaker in the aftermath

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:13.660
of her break-up with the Joker — via the
reveal of a fresh trailer.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:18.660
Harley Quinn, voiced by The Big Bang Theory's
Kaley Cuoco, endeavors to carve her own path

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:23.180
of chaos and crime in the streets of Gotham
without the shadow of her former flame looming

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:23.720
overhead.

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:29.220
To do so, she crosses paths with some major
DC Comics players, as well as a few New 52

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:33.900
pals, such as Sy Borgman, an elderly cyborg
voiced by Seinfeld's Jason Alexander.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:35.640
Her ultimate goal?

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:39.100
Become a member of the supervillain alliance
known as the Legion of Doom.

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:44.680
With hammers swinging, money falling, drinks
clinking, punches and kicks flying, plus plenty

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:48.900
of expletives being tossed around, the Harley
Quinn trailer proves that anyone who tunes

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:53.340
into the series will see the up-and-coming
criminal Queenpin of Gotham City in a brand-new

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:53.920
way.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:58.520
And, while they're at it, they'll get to catch
Harley taking down famed DC comics vigilantes

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:03.940
like Aquaman and, of course, Batman, voiced
by Diedrich Bader, returning to the role after

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:06.520
2008's Brave and the Bold animated series.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:11.560
“That petulant primate’s poisonous plot
must be prevented!"

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:16.400
Harley Quinn features an impressive cast of
familiar voices, including Tony Hale as Doctor

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:21.160
Psycho, Christopher Meloni as Commissioner
James Gordon, and Wanda Sykes as The Queen

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:21.760
of Fables.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:26.180
This isn't the first of Harley Quinn that
we've seen — a fourth-wall-breaking teaser

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:31.439
dropped during New York Comic-Con in October
of 2018, featuring a DC-fandom-dissing Poison

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:31.940
Ivy ...

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:34.440
"I think they're going to hate it, Harls.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:35.440
They hate everything."

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:36.440
"No way!

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:39.780
It's got comedy, action, incredibly gratuitous
violence …"

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:44.680
By the looks of this new trailer, it seems
Harley Quinn will only get wilder as the first

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:45.580
season rolls out.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.860
Lead voice actress Cuoco has teased that viewers
are in for an R-rated ride when the show premieres.

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:54.460
Posting the Harley Quinn trailer to her Instagram
page, Cuoco wrote,

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:56.600
"This show is gonna blow your minds!

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:01.840
Way [too] much fun!!! (and a tad R-rated)
#harleyquinn coming soon! [...] also the [Joker]

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:03.260
has an emoji but Harley doesn't!!?

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:04.660
She's gonna be pissed!"

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:09.820
The raunchy Harley Quinn animated series certainly
feels like a shock to the DC system, but it

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:14.940
actually comes after a few other legitimately
R-rated animated projects based on DC Comics

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:15.460
characters.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:20.500
The 2017 feature Justice League Dark, based
on the comic of the same name, rocked the

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:21.020
R rating.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:26.860
So too did 2018's Gotham by Gaslight, as well
as 2016's Batman: The Killing Joke.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:31.260
The most recent R-rated animated flick to
come from Warner Bros. actually includes the

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:32.840
Cupid of Crime herself.

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:38.700
2018's Suicide Squad: Hell to Pay sees Amanda
Waller assembling a brand-new Task Force X

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:42.840
roster, with Harley Quinn and company hunting
down the coveted "Get Out of Hell Free" card.

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:47.460
So, while DC Universe's upcoming Harley Quinn
show is certainly going to drop some jaws

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:51.630
and widen some eyes, it follows a handful
of other adult-aimed animated flicks that

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:53.300
exist in the same comic book realm.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:58.420
Perhaps reception to the new series will be
so strong that it motivates Warner Bros. Animation

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:02.780
to greenlight additional series in the same
vein as Harley Quinn — maybe even some focused

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:06.700
on groups like the Suicide Squad or the Birds
of Prey, both of which have had Harley on

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:07.260
board.

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:12.320
Only time will tell if the R-rated Harley
Quinn becomes DC's animated answer to Marvel's

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:15.700
Deadpool, or just a failed experiment in envelope-pushing.

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:18.240
"Harley?"

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:18.920
"It's me, d--khead!"

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:19.520
"Ahoy!"

